==Strategy==
It is recommended to get extra money from the first peons with cats like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. You can cheese this stage with Unit Attack UP and money-related [[Cat Combo|Combos]], Can Can Cat (Money Up and Move Speed Up Talents) and rusher-type units, such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], or [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]. If you don't wish to cheese it, [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] will destroy this stage. You may also want to use [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] and/or [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune units]]. Try not to take too much time against Le'mammoth, or else the Midnite Ds, Lutrinae Gokurakkos, and Bore Jrs. can be annoying.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusives such as [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]], [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]] and [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolic Gao]] are Immune to Waves and can get massive damage on the enemies. For units that don't outrange Le'mammoth, you'll want to utilize things like the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] Cannon to land attacks more consistently. This includes [[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]] and [[Moonshade Kaworu (Legend Rare Cat)|Moon Disciple Kaworu]].
*[[Mass Production EVA (Uber Rare Cat)|Mass Production Eva]]: With 410 range, they outrange every enemy on this stage (though they outrange Le'mammoth only by 10). In addition, they possess Wave Immunity and can Freeze both Angel and Traitless enemies.

==Trivia==
*The Japanese names of Furious Field and [[Mirage Meadow]] are puns. Both have the word ''kyozō'' in their names, but written with different kanji to form different meanings. Furious Field spells ''kyozō'' as 巨象, meaning "[[Le'mammoth|giant elephant]]", whereas Mirage Meadow uses 虚像, referring to a [[wikipedia:Virtual image|virtual image]].

